    {
      "text": "Dunsparce has a drill for its tail. It uses this tail to burrow into the ground backward. This Pokémon is known to make its nest in complex shapes deep under the ground.",
      "version": "omega-ruby"
    },
    {
      "text": "Dunsparce has a drill for its tail. It uses this tail to burrow into the ground backward. This Pokémon is known to make its nest in complex shapes deep under the ground.",
      "version": "alpha-sapphire"
    },
    {
      "text": "It travels by digging through the ground. Diglett and Dunsparce share one another’s tunnels happily.",
      "version": "ultra-sun"
    },
    {
      "text": "When it sees a person, it digs a hole with its tail to make its escape. If you happen to find one, consider yourself lucky.",
      "version": "ultra-moon"
    },
    {
      "text": "This Pokémon’s tiny wings have some scientists saying that Dunsparce used to fly through the sky in ancient times.",
      "version": "sword"
    },
    {
      "text": "The nests Dunsparce live in are mazes of tunnels. They never get lost in their own nests—they can tell where they are by the scent of the dirt.",
      "version": "shield"
    }
